# ArbitrageX v2 — backup recipient age public key (EXAMPLE).
#
# Paste your operator age public key below (format: age1...). Only the
# corresponding age private key — kept offline by the operator — can decrypt
# the backups produced by automation/scripts/backup-pg.sh.
#
# Generate your keypair:
#   age-keygen -o arbx-backup.age.identity
#   grep '^# public key:' arbx-backup.age.identity
#
# Store arbx-backup.age.identity OFFLINE (hardware key, offline laptop, paper
# print). NEVER commit it. The public key below is safe to commit.
#
# Rotate the keypair annually or on suspected leak. After rotation, the old
# backups stop being readable with the new key — keep the old identity until
# you've proved all backups newer than the rotation are restorable.
#
# The deployed file at configs/backup-recipient.age.pub is read by the
# operator's own deployment tooling and fed to backup-pg.sh via the
# AGE_RECIPIENT env var.

age1REPLACE_ME_WITH_OPERATOR_PUBLIC_KEY
